title: The Party After Heidelberg
subtitle: The congress did not split the party. Now it must be led.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month >= 11 and crisis = 0 and heidelberg_outcome >= 2
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: kapd_split = 0

= The Party After Heidelberg

[? if heidelberg_outcome = 2 : The party has kept its members and lost its peace. Laufenberg's Hamburg paper attacks the Zentrale every week, and Levi complains that he cannot make a decision without a Left Radical veto. ?][? if heidelberg_outcome = 3 : The new Zentrale has moved its office to Hamburg and told the members to tear up their union cards. Levi's friends in Halle, Thuringia and Saxony are holding meetings of their own, and the Independents are courting them. ?]

- @discipline: Cut off the subsidies of districts that boycott the unions.
- @share: Give Wolffheim a seat in the Zentrale.
- @offer: Offer the Spartacists their seats back.
- @purge: Remove the "parliamentarians" from the district committees.

@discipline
subtitle: Less peace, more party. The Left Radicals will stay, for now.
view-if: heidelberg_outcome = 2
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction -= 8; unity -= 4; lean_luxemburgist += 2

The Left Radicals call it blackmail.

@share
subtitle: The meetings will be longer and the decisions vaguer. The party will not split.
view-if: heidelberg_outcome = 2
on-arrival: ultraleft_satisfaction += 8; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4; unity += 6; lean_unionist += 2

@offer
subtitle: Unity first. The Left Radicals in the districts will call it surrender.
view-if: heidelberg_outcome = 3
on-arrival: luxemburgist_satisfaction += 15; unionist_satisfaction += 6; ultraleft_satisfaction -= 6; unity += 6

Levi refuses a seat for himself but lets two of his friends accept.

@purge
subtitle: The Spartacists may leave. Lenin will hear of it.
view-if: heidelberg_outcome = 3
on-arrival: {!
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 15;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 10;
Q.unity -= 6;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
RG.ecci('lenin', -6);
!}

Officials who sat on union committees are removed. In Halle and Chemnitz the members re-elect them the next week.
